Codex CLI

Install:
  Install the global Codex CLI if needed; prepare Node/pnpm and configure PATH.

Upgrade:
  Update the installed Codex CLI; prepare Node/pnpm as needed.

Status:
  Read the locally available Codex CLI version.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  PNPM_HOME: reuse the persisted Node environment; default ~/.local/share/pnpm
  Open a new terminal after installation to load PATH changes.
  Run codex to sign in; authentication is managed by Codex.
